## ERPForAll addon development

Before writing or changing an ERPForAll addon, read the matching skill file (each starts with a
short procedure and ends with its sources). The skills live in `{{KIT}}/skills/`.

- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-addon-tests/SKILL.md`: Test an ERPForAll addon - static lint, install into a database, native Rust tests with erp_testkit::Harness and registry builds, manifest consistency tests, and Elang component tests for client code. Use when asked to verify an addon works, add tests, or debug a failing install.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-chatter/SKILL.md`: Add the chatter (messages, followers, activities) to a model and its form in an ERPForAll addon - depend on mail, inherit mail.thread, place <chatter/> in the form view, post messages from code. Use when a record needs a discussion thread, followers or notes.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-client-extensions/SKILL.md`: Add web client code to an ERPForAll addon - a custom field widget, a control-panel extension, templates and styles declared in static/client.json, registries and patches in the Elang client. Use when a view needs a widget or UI behaviour that the built-in widgets do not give.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-create-addon/SKILL.md`: Create a new ERPForAll addon from scratch - manifest.toml, directory layout, data-only versus native (Rust) addon, scaffolding, listing data files, installing it into a database. Use when the user asks to start, scaffold or register a new ERPForAll addon or module.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-data-files/SKILL.md`: Write ERPForAll data files - XML records, external ids, ref/eval/search values, noupdate, CSV files, default data every model must ship, and demo data. Use when adding seed or default records, demo records, or when a data file fails to load.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-extend-addon/SKILL.md`: Extend an existing ERPForAll addon from a new addon - add fields to someone else's model, add a column or field to their form, add access rows, without editing the original. Use for requests like "add a field to the contact form" or "customize the product addon".
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-for-odoo-developers/SKILL.md`: Map Odoo concepts to ERPForAll - manifest, models, inheritance, api decorators, access rows and rules, views, data files, server actions, RPC - and the places where ERPForAll deliberately differs or fails loudly. Use when the user knows Odoo and asks how to do something the ERPForAll way.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-menus-actions/SKILL.md`: Add menus and window actions to an ERPForAll addon - ir.actions.act_window records, view_mode, linking specific views, <menuitem> trees, groups, icons, root menus and settings entries. Use when the user wants an app menu, a menu entry, or an action that opens a model's list or form.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-models-fields/SKILL.md`: Declare ERPForAll models and fields - TOML model files for data-only addons and the #[model] / #[field] / #[extend] macros for native Rust addons, field types and keys, relations, defaults, constraints and computed fields. Use when adding or changing a model, a field or a relation in an addon.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-security/SKILL.md`: Set access control for an ERPForAll addon - security/ir.access.csv rows (permissions and restrictions), res.groups records, field-level groups, record domains with user.id and company_ids. Use when a model needs access rights, per-user or per-company record rules, or a custom group.
- `{{KIT}}/skills/erpforall-views/SKILL.md`: Write ERPForAll views - list, form and search XML in ir.ui.view records under the <erp> root, header buttons, groups and notebooks, field widgets, and extending another addon's view with xpath/position inheritance. Use when adding or changing a screen, a column, a filter or a form layout.

Tools (Python 3.11+): `python3 {{KIT}}/tools/new-addon.py <name> --dest addons` scaffolds a data-only
addon; `python3 {{KIT}}/tools/addon-lint.py addons/<name> --addons-path addons` checks one.
If a skill does not cover something, say so; do not invent APIs, XML attributes or CLI flags.
